{#- The olim's own door, at `/aliyah` (targum-internal#385, 2026-09-29).

    The front door speaks to every learner at once, and David kept it that way. This is
    the page for one of them: somebody living in Israel, or on the way, whose ulpan ended
    and whose Hebrew stopped where it did. It says so in its first line, and it is the
    address a post in an olim group carries.

    Drawn from the front door's own parts and its one stylesheet, and held to the same
    rules: everything is baked in, nothing is fetched (§11), and the waitlist's form is a
    plain post that works with JavaScript off. It carries no script at all: nothing on it
    moves. Since 2026-10-02 it is drawn from the rebuilt front door (#555): the hero with
    a card beside it, the cards of "How you learn", the band of tiles on ink, and the
    waitlist as the ending, so the two pages read as one site.

    What it leaves out is on purpose. No Torah, no "one list, from Genesis to the news":
    the GTM note had already said that line reads as "bible tool" to an oleh.

    Every claim is one the product keeps today: a photo of a page and a screenshot of a
    chat both become a text (`ingest/pages.py`). -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
{% include '_public_head.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('landing.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
{{ chrome_face() }}
</head>
<body class="landing">
{#- The bar's places are the front door's, so `home` is its address: this page has no
    parts by those names, and the front door is where they are. -#}
{% with bar_class = 'bar', home = '/', here = '/aliyah' %}{% include '_front_bar.html.j2' %}{% endwith %}

<main id="top">
  {#- The hero as the front door draws it, with its one call to action, the waitlist,
      where the front door has its box; beside it, where the front door's word card
      stands, four lines an oleh is sent. -#}
  <div class="col top olim">
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="headline">
        <h1>{{ t("aliyah.page.learn-hebrew-from-your-own-life-in-israel", "Learn Hebrew from your own life in Israel.") }}</h1>
        <p class="lede">{{ t("aliyah.page.bring-a-video-a-voice-note-or-a", "Bring a video, a voice note or a photo of a letter. Every line arrives with vowels and English.") }}</p>
        {%- if not signed_in|default(false) %}
        {% include '_join_form.html.j2' %}
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      <ul class="facts">
        <li>{{ t("aliyah.page.for-after-ulpan", "For after ulpan") }}</li>
        <li>{{ t("landing.page.upload-any-text-or-media", "Upload any text or media") }}</li>
        <li>{{ t("landing.page.hundreds-of-free-texts-and-videos", "Hundreds of free texts and videos") }}</li>
        <li>{{ t("landing.page.no-credit-card-required", "No credit card required") }}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    {#- Four lines of the Hebrew an oleh is sent, one from each part of the week: money,
        school, home and health. The Hebrew is the page's own and stands here pointed;
        what is under each line goes through the catalogue. -#}
    <figure class="letters" aria-label="{{ t("aliyah.page.examples-hebrew-from-everyday-life", "Examples: Hebrew from everyday life") }}">
      <div class="letter">
        <span class="label">{{ t("aliyah.page.from-the-bank", "From the bank") }}</span>
        <p class="he">כַּרְטִיס חָדָשׁ נִשְׁלַח אֵלֶיךָ בַּדֹּאַר.</p>
        <p class="letter-en">{{ t("aliyah.page.a-new-card-was-sent-to-you-by", "A new card was sent to you by post.") }}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="letter">
        <span class="label">{{ t("aliyah.page.from-the-school", "From the school") }}</span>
        <p class="he">מָחָר אֵין לִמּוּדִים.</p>
        <p class="letter-en">{{ t("aliyah.page.there-is-no-school-tomorrow", "There is no school tomorrow.") }}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="letter">
        <span class="label">{{ t("aliyah.page.from-the-building", "From the building") }}</span>
        <p class="he">הַמַּעֲלִית לֹא תַּעֲבֹד מָחָר בַּבֹּקֶר.</p>
        <p class="letter-en">{{ t("aliyah.page.the-lift-will-not-work-tomorrow-morning", "The lift will not work tomorrow morning.") }}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="letter">
        <span class="label">{{ t("aliyah.page.from-the-clinic", "From the clinic") }}</span>
        <p class="he">הַתּוֹר שֶׁלְּךָ בְּיוֹם שְׁלִישִׁי בְּשָׁעָה עֶשֶׂר.</p>
        <p class="letter-en">{{ t("aliyah.page.your-appointment-is-on-tuesday-at-ten", "Your appointment is on Tuesday at ten.") }}</p>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <section class="part" id="after-ulpan">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("aliyah.page.after-ulpan", "After ulpan") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("aliyah.page.ulpan-ended-your-hebrew-can-keep-going", "Ulpan ended. Your Hebrew can keep going.") }}</h2>
        <p>{{ t("aliyah.page.you-get-by-in-english-and-the-hebrew", "You get by in English, and the Hebrew around you stays just out of reach. targum starts from that Hebrew, and from the words you already know.") }}</p>
      </div>
      {#- The four moments that send an oleh looking, as the front door's "How you learn"
          cards, two by two. -#}
      <ul class="how four">
        <li class="how-card">
          <h3>{{ t("aliyah.page.start-where-ulpan-stopped", "Start where ulpan stopped") }}</h3>
          <p>{{ t("aliyah.page.tell-us-how-much-hebrew-you-know-and", "Tell us how much Hebrew you know, and tick off the words you have. Everything is sorted from there, so you never begin at aleph again.") }}</p>
        </li>
        <li class="how-card">
          <h3>{{ t("aliyah.page.read-what-arrives", "Read what arrives") }}</h3>
          <p>{{ t("aliyah.page.a-letter-from-the-bank-a-message-from", "A letter from the bank, a message from the school, a notice in the stairwell. Take a photo or a screenshot, and read it line by line.") }}</p>
        </li>
        <li class="how-card">
          <h3>{{ t("aliyah.page.follow-what-everyone-is-talking-about", "Follow what everyone is talking about") }}</h3>
          <p>{{ t("aliyah.page.this-week-s-news-in-easy-hebrew-and", "This week’s news in easy Hebrew, and any video or podcast you paste a link to, with every word one tap away.") }}</p>
        </li>
        <li class="how-card">
          <h3>{{ t("aliyah.page.made-for-adults", "Made for adults") }}</h3>
          <p>{{ t("aliyah.page.no-points-and-no-drills-you-read-real", "No points and no drills. You read real Hebrew, and we keep count of every word you learn.") }}</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="part" id="your-own">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.page.your-own-hebrew", "Your own Hebrew") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("aliyah.page.if-it-arrived-in-hebrew-you-can-read", "If it arrived in Hebrew, you can read it here.") }}</h2>
        <p>{{ t("landing.page.paste-a-link-or-drop-a-file-whatever", "Paste a link or drop a file. Recordings are written out word by word and timed to the voice, so each word lights up as it’s said.") }}</p>
      </div>
      {% include '_bring_band.html.j2' %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="part" id="questions">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.page.questions", "Questions") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("landing.page.before-you-join", "Before you join.") }}</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq">
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.is-targum-for-me", "Is targum for me?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("aliyah.page.if-you-live-in-israel-or-are-on", "If you live in Israel, or are on your way, and know the alphabet, yes. It’s made for the point where ulpan or an app stops: you know the letters and some words, and the Hebrew around you is still too hard.") }}</p></details>
        <details><summary>{{ t("aliyah.page.can-i-bring-a-letter-or-a-message", "Can I bring a letter or a message?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("aliyah.page.yes-take-a-photo-of-the-letter-or", "Yes. Take a photo of the letter or a screenshot of the chat, and add it. We write out the Hebrew with its vowels and put English under every line.") }}</p></details>
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.is-what-i-bring-private", "Is what I bring private?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.page.yes-what-you-bring-is-yours-and-we", "Yes. What you bring is yours, and we never train a model on it.") }}</p></details>
        <details><summary>{{ t("aliyah.page.does-it-replace-ulpan", "Does it replace ulpan?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.page.it-s-the-other-half-of-one-a", "It’s the other half of one. A course teaches you the rules; targum gives you real Hebrew to practise them on, every day, and keeps count of every word you learn.") }}</p></details>
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.what-will-it-cost", "What will it cost?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.page.the-library-is-free-to-read-and-stays", "The library is free to read and stays free. There’ll be a paid plan for reading your own Hebrew: the videos, podcasts and books you bring us.") }}</p></details>
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.when-does-it-open", "When does it open?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.page.we-re-opening-in-small-groups-rather-than", "We’re opening in small groups. Join the waitlist and we’ll email you when your turn comes.") }}</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- The front door's ending. Not to somebody who has already chosen targum (§6; copy
      audit, 2026-09-28). -#}
  {%- if not signed_in|default(false) %}
  {% include '_join_end.html.j2' %}
  {%- endif %}
</main>

{% with signin = true %}{% include '_public_foot.html.j2' %}{% endwith %}
</body>
</html>
